## Decoder API reconciliation

- The reverse public-surface scan found `DecodeLimits` and
  `decompress_limited` exposed caller-adjustable bounds with no matching pinned
  Java public API. The Phase 8 safety requirement remains in place through
  fixed internal bounds: 16 MiB per record, 64 MiB per decompressed body, and
  64 MiB aggregate decoded data.
- Public `decode_one` and `decode_many` now take only their record(s) and
  `DecodeOptions`; `DecodeLimits` is private to the common decoder. The bounded
  decompression helper is crate-internal, and public `decompress` uses the
  fixed 64 MiB output cap. Pull-result and POP paths no longer accept limit
  arguments. Inner-batch decoding keeps equivalent private bounds.
- Moved low-cap decode/decompression regressions into common-crate unit tests.
  Updated cross-crate callers, the fuzz harness, benchmark, Phase 8 API matrix,
  and release checklist. This closes the decoder API discrepancy only;
  P18-V01's full source/input/overload/reverse-export audit remains open.

